  "strategy": "1.Approach and rationale:\n   The central idea is to employ a hybrid optimization strategy combining local refinement and stochastic search to escape local minima. The bottleneck is the high likelihood of getting stuck in suboptimal solutions using SLSQP alone. This approach builds upon the provided parent solution but introduces:\n   - Multi-resolution exploration across different grid sizes\n   - Simulated annealing for global exploration\n   - Custom gradient-based refinement using overlapping windows\n   - Progressive upsampling with cost-effective hyperparameter adaptation\n   The rationale is that addressing both local and global optimization simultaneously can yield solutions with smaller overlap integrals. This leverages the convexity of certain sections while mitigating premature convergence.\n\n2.Mathematicalspecification:\n   Variables:\n     - h: Discrete samples of step function values\n     - n_points: Current resolution\n     - k: Discrete shift index\n   Objective:\n     - Minimize C5 = max_k\u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n   Over its discrete approximation:\n     - C5 = max_k[ np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\")[k] * (2.0/n_points) ]\n   Representation:\n     - Vector of values in [0,1] with sum = n_points/2\n   Algorithm components:\n     a) Local refinement using projected gradients against worst shift\n     b) Global SA using piecewise linear moves with directed crossover\n     c) Multiscale analysis - optimizing parents at scale factors [0.2, 0.3, 0.4]\n   Constraints:\n     - Feasibility maintained via repair operations\n     - Hyperparameters adapt during optimization based on scale\n\n3.Implementationprocedure:\n   Stage 1: Initialization\n     - Input: parent vector (if available) or random continuous function\n     - Scale-dependent repair: adjust sum and bounds\n     - Balancing between continuity (piecewise constant) and flexibility\n   Stage 2: Local refinement\n     - Compute shift powers while controlling gradient scale\n     - Temperature-based windowed iteration\n   Stage 3: Global search\n     - SA moves using concentration matrix of overlap values\n     - Temporal acceptance criteria favoring higher overlap\n   Stage 4: Progressive upsample\n     - Iterative doubling with normalization\n     - Cost estimate based on current scale factor\n   Stage 5: Termination\n     - Timely checkpointing\n     - Memory prioritization\n     - Repair fallback if objective saturates\n\n4.Searchchoicesandusefulvariations:\n   a) Initial configuration:\n      - Beta schedule: [20, 150, 250, 400]\n      - SA acceptance: initial T = 0.1 * current C5\n      - Window sizes: [3, 5, 7] during refinement\n   b) Scale factor adaptation:\n      - Progressive: 0.2 \u2192 0.3 \u2192 0.4 \u2192 0.6 scales\n      - Recall time: O(n_points) \u2248 30 samples\n   c) Recovery fallback:\n      - Resample previous best solution\n      - Repair using median extrapolation\n   d) Variation conditions:\n      - Refinement: \u0393_max = 100 (grid steps)\n      - Upsample: n_last > 120 and improvement < \u03b4 = 0.0002\n\n5.Computebudgetandrobustness:\n   - Dominant cost: SA and progressive upsampling\n   - Estimated time: 800s scaling (n_points=120 to 720)\n   - Agile execution:\n     - *Pause* solver calls every 500ms with budget monitoring\n     - If stuck: switch to gradient-mode with halved window\n     - Memory: prioritize storing best-of-last-5 solutions\n   - Restart protocol:\n     - If no improvement for 200 steps: repair and rerun segment\n\n6.Validationandreturncontract:\n   a) Feasibility checks:\n     - All entries \u2208 [0,1]\n     - Sum adjustment within tolerance\n     - Objective calculation via direct correlation\n   b) Termination criteria:\n     - Elapsed budget (90% mark)\n     - Convergence plateau (\u03c8=0.00001)\n   c) Implementation safeguards:\n     - Repair mechanism: resize via interpolation\n     - Accuracy check: verify cross-term computations\n     - Output contract: [(h_values), C5(float), n_points(int)]\n   d) Failure response:\n     - Return last verified solution\n     - Print deprecation notice\n     -Fallback: [600 samples] with equal pattern",
